msgid "Wind Speed Monitor settings - help"
msgstr "Настройки монитора скорости ветра - помощь"

#: plugins/wind_monitor/templates/wind_monitor_help.html:10
msgid ""
"The plug-in measures wind with a PCF8583 event counter at I2C address 0x50 or "
"0x51. It can stop selected stations, send an e-mail or run a program when "
"confirmed wind thresholds are exceeded."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/wind_monitor/templates/wind_monitor_help.html:12
msgid ""
"Each measurement resets the counter, waits approximately ten seconds and "
"divides the pulse count by the actual monotonic elapsed time. This prevents I2C "
"lock waiting from incorrectly increasing the calculated wind speed."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/wind_monitor/templates/wind_monitor_help.html:13
msgid ""
"The PCF8583 counter bytes are read directly from registers 0x01 to 0x03 and "
"every BCD digit is validated. A failed setup, short read or invalid digit is "
"rejected."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/wind_monitor/templates/wind_monitor_help.html:14
msgid ""
"The plausibility filter rejects speeds above the configured maximum accepted "
"speed. Rejected values do not change the current or maximum speed and cannot be "
"logged or trigger an automatic action."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/wind_monitor/templates/wind_monitor_help.html:15
msgid ""
"Station stopping and e-mail notification require the configured number of "
"consecutive accepted threshold exceedances. Program actions retain their "
"separate exceedance count and time interval."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/wind_monitor/templates/wind_monitor_help.html:16
msgid ""
"The trend compares older and newer samples from approximately the last minute. "
"The arrow shows rising, falling or steady wind after enough samples have been "
"collected."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/wind_monitor/templates/wind_monitor_help.html:17
msgid ""
"I2C diagnostic logging records setup, retries, raw counter bytes, actual "
"elapsed time, pulse rate, calculated speed and rejection reason. The file is "
"size limited and rotated automatically. Enable it only while investigating a "
"problem."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/wind_monitor/templates/wind_monitor_help.html:18
msgid ""
"Decimal calibration and threshold values accept both a decimal point and a "
"decimal comma."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/wind_monitor/templates/wind_monitor_help.html:19
msgid ""
"One meter per second equals 3.6 kilometers per hour. Measurement accuracy "
"depends on the pulses-per-rotation and speed-per-rotation calibration."
msgstr ""

